1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,865
Isla Lagarto: an island of prehistoric proportions, and home to The Raptor Games.

2
00:00:05,085 --> 00:00:06,835
Here's how the location plays.

3
00:00:07,667 --> 00:00:11,765
Each Setup card shows the three Electric Fence sections in green or red.

4
00:00:11,765 --> 00:00:15,067
Put a fence marker on each green section, and none on red.

5
00:00:15,067 --> 00:00:18,141
In this example, A and C get markers and B stays open.

6
00:00:18,361 --> 00:00:22,265
Shuffle the three Lava cards face down, with the Lava tokens beside them.

7
00:00:22,485 --> 00:00:25,664
Put the T-Rex card out with the T-Rex meeple on its Start space.

8
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:28,831
There are three Electric Fences, A, B and C.

9
00:00:28,831 --> 00:00:33,174
While a fence marker is on a path, nobody can move along it, and the spaces either

10
00:00:33,174 --> 00:00:34,287
side aren't adjacent.

11
00:00:34,507 --> 00:00:37,088
Anyone panicking into a fence just stays where they are.

12
00:00:37,308 --> 00:00:40,971
In every Upkeep the power fluctuates: roll the Electric Fence die.

13
00:00:40,971 --> 00:00:44,135
If that fence has a marker, remove it. If not, place one.

14
00:00:44,967 --> 00:00:49,372
When working out the closest or farthest target, only count paths not blocked by

15
00:00:49,372 --> 00:00:53,997
fences. If every fence is up and the only target is beyond them, measure as if there

16
00:00:53,997 --> 00:00:54,823
were no fences.

17
00:00:55,043 --> 00:00:59,486
If an Enemy has no open path to its target, it doesn't move, but still resolves its

18
00:00:59,486 --> 00:01:00,824
attacks in its own space.

19
00:01:01,044 --> 00:01:03,156
Effects that place someone ignore fences.

20
00:01:03,967 --> 00:01:08,651
The T-Rex starts locked in the Dino Pen. Each time you see the T-Rex icon, move its

21
00:01:08,651 --> 00:01:11,135
meeple one space right along the T-Rex card.

22
00:01:11,355 --> 00:01:15,812
When it reaches Break Out!, put the T-Rex on the board in the Dino Pen, and the

23
00:01:15,812 --> 00:01:19,311
T-Rex Action token below the Killer Action on the Finale card.

24
00:01:19,311 --> 00:01:20,891
Ignore any more T-Rex icons.

25
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:25,784
The T-Rex isn't a Killer or a Minion, and can't be attacked, damaged or killed.

26
00:01:25,784 --> 00:01:28,783
It acts after the Minion and Killer Actions on the Finale.

27
00:01:29,003 --> 00:01:33,113
It moves two spaces, but stops as soon as it reaches a space with anyone in it:

28
00:01:33,113 --> 00:01:37,224
you, Victims or Enemies. And it won't move at all if anyone shares its starting

29
00:01:37,224 --> 00:01:37,536
space.

30
00:01:37,756 --> 00:01:41,829
Victims won't follow you into its space, and in the Panic phase everyone in its

31
00:01:41,829 --> 00:01:43,943
space panics, whether or not anyone died.

32
00:01:44,767 --> 00:01:48,962
The T-Rex doesn't do damage. It instantly kills one target in its space, choosing a

33
00:01:48,962 --> 00:01:51,743
Victim first, then a Minion, then you, then the Killer.

34
00:01:51,963 --> 00:01:55,963
If it picks you or the Killer, that's an instant kill, without revealing a Final

35
00:01:55,963 --> 00:01:56,613
Health token.

36
00:01:56,833 --> 00:02:00,764
Against groups like the Raptor Pack or a Zombie Horde, it kills one unit:

37
00:02:00,764 --> 00:02:01,356
one damage.

38
00:02:02,167 --> 00:02:04,899
The first volcano icon makes the Volcano erupt.

39
00:02:04,899 --> 00:02:09,491
Everyone there takes damage, anyone left panics, and you place the Volcano Lava

40
00:02:09,491 --> 00:02:12,513
token. That space is closed to everyone from now on.

41
00:02:12,733 --> 00:02:15,533
Each later icon spreads lava to an adjacent space:

42
00:02:15,533 --> 00:02:18,724
draw a Lava card and follow it. North Beach, for example:

43
00:02:18,724 --> 00:02:23,315
everyone there is hurt, survivors panic until they leave, and the North Beach Lava

44
00:02:23,315 --> 00:02:24,211
token goes down.

45
00:02:24,431 --> 00:02:28,398
Once all four Lava tokens are out, ignore further volcano icons.

46
00:02:28,398 --> 00:02:32,303
Lava spaces are closed to everyone, Raptors and T-Rex included.

47
00:02:33,133 --> 00:02:37,394
The three corner spaces with the beach icon are Beaches, and the two edge spaces

48
00:02:37,394 --> 00:02:40,429
with the cliff icon are Cliffs. Some cards refer to them.

49
00:02:40,649 --> 00:02:44,740
Holy Mosasaurus! attacks the space with the most Victims and Enemies, hurting

50
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:48,884
everyone there. Power Surge puts every fence up and skips the next fence roll.

51
00:02:49,104 --> 00:02:53,398
The Tranquilizer Gun can be used any time to deal one damage to an adjacent Enemy,

52
00:02:53,398 --> 00:02:55,440
and ends its movement if it was moving.

53
00:02:56,267 --> 00:03:00,448
A few tips. Fences change every Upkeep, so check them before you plan a route.

54
00:03:00,668 --> 00:03:05,027
Once the T-Rex is loose, lure the Killer into its path and stay out of it yourself.

55
00:03:05,027 --> 00:03:07,495
Bait draws Enemies and the T-Rex onto the Goat.

56
00:03:07,715 --> 00:03:10,337
Search spaces are close together here, which helps.

57
00:03:10,337 --> 00:03:10,851
Good luck.

